    "Thunder Burger & Bar (Georgetown)": "A rock-and-roll Georgetown bar whose Love Me Tender stacks a kobe beef patty with white cheddar and sweet housemade remoulade on toasted brioche.",
    "Stoney's On P (Logan Circle)": "A fifty-year-old community bar open late, known for the Texas burger with crispy bacon, creamy coleslaw, and tangy barbecue sauce.",
    "Ben's Chili Bowl (U Street)": "A 1958 DC institution best known for half-smokes but also serving a classic chili cheeseburger steeped in civil-rights-era history.",
    "Any Day Now (Navy Yard)": "Tim Ma's Navy Yard cafe nests a beef patty between two crispy scallion pancakes with lettuce, pickles, onions, and special sauce.",
