    "Sanford Stadium (Athens, Georgia; 93,033)": "Georgia’s storied bowl “between the hedges,” ringed by the privet that has framed Bulldog football since 1929. One of the largest and loudest stadiums in the South.",
    "Cotton Bowl (Dallas, Texas; 92,100)": "The Fair Park landmark in Dallas that gave the Cotton Bowl Classic its name and hosts the Red River Rivalry between Texas and Oklahoma each October. A 1930s relic expanded over the decades into a six-figure-capacity venue."
